# Local credentials. The pre-flight run in cloud-sync/README.md tells you to create cloud-sync/.env
# holding CF_API_TOKEN, which is a token that can write every row in the catalogue — so this rule is
# the difference between a secret on one machine and a secret in the repository history. `.env.example`
# is the committed template and must stay un-ignored, which is why these are file names, not `.env*`.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.qoder/
preflight-*.json
preflight-*.txt
pre-dedupe.sql
